 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S445-002\", \"clauses\": {\"present_data\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F09\", \"template\": \"Create a {bg_full_lbl} to show: {data_str}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F09 asks the learner to create a graph from a generated data set. Its bg_full_lbl slot can print F01 (bar graph), which reads correctly, so the task of presenting data is produced.\"}, \"data_set\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F08\", \"template\": \"Complete the table to show: {data_str}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F08 prints the generated data set as category and value pairs. The observed printed values are all whole numbers from 5 to 70 with readable categories (grades, months, subjects, fruits, sports, pets, flowers, days).\"}, \"data_table\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F08\", \"template\": \"Complete the table to show: {data_str}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F08 asks the learner to complete a table, which addresses the tables representation. Its only domain is the data_str repeat, and the table word is in cumulative_vocab.\"}, \"single_bar_graph\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F09\", \"template\": \"Create a {bg_full_lbl} to show: {data_str}.\", \"reasoning\": \"When bg_full_lbl takes the F01 member, the question reads as a request to create a bar graph with no orientation word. This is a single bar graph, and the bar graph and single bar graph wording is introduced by this lc.\"}, \"horizontal_bar_graph\": {\"verdict\": \"NOT_PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": null, \"template\": null, \"reasoning\": \"The only orientation word is the F10 member of the bg_full_lbl domain. F10 prints just the orientation word with a trailing space, and F09 places it where the graph noun should be, so no readable problem names a horizontal bar graph. The horizontal (x-axis) text in F06 is a hint about an axis, not a graph orientation.\"}, \"vertical_bar_graph\": {\"verdict\": \"NOT_PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": null, \"template\": null, \"reasoning\": \"The only orientation word is the F10 member of the bg_full_lbl domain. F10 prints just the orientation word with a trailing space, and F09 places it where the graph noun should be, so no readable problem names a vertical bar graph. The vertical (y-axis) text in F07 is a hint about an axis, not a graph orientation.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F05\", \"F06\", \"F07\", \"F09\", \"F10\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"The {scale_label} on the {axis} goes up by {scale}.\", \"horizontal (x-axis)\", \"vertical (y-axis)\", \"Create a {bg_full_lbl} to show: {data_str}.\", \"{orientation} \"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F09 draws bg_full_lbl from F01 or F10. The F10 member prints only an orientation word, so F09 can produce a question with no graph noun, which is wrong and unreadable. F10 is therefore at fault as well. F05 draws its axis from F06 or F07 with no link to the orientation, so a hint can name the horizontal (x-axis) for a vertical graph or the vertical (y-axis) for a horizontal graph, which is misleading. The x-axis and y-axis wording in F06 and F07 is not in cumulative_vocab or introduces_vocab, though axis is. F04 (bar graph hint) and F01/F02/F03 pass.\"}",
